{"mls":"R1682858","addr":"413 North Main Street","muni":"Jamestown city","town":"Jamestown","county":"Chautauqua","zip":"14701","ll":[42.097812,-79.242079],"status":"Active","type":"Single Family","units":1,"beds":6,"baths":3,"sqft":9097.0,"year":1886,"lot":0.276,"dom":43,"price":299900,"orig":null,"chg":"Back On Market","tax":9301,"tax_mls":true,"hoa":null,"office":"Century 21 Turner Brokers","phone":"danterhune@c21turnerbrokers.com","hhp":false,"remarks":"Here is your chance to own a piece of Jamestown’s history. This property is known as the Tew Mansion, it was built in the late 1800’s by Milton Earl Beebe, for George Washington Tew, who was the President of the City National Bank in the late 1880’s. Over the years, this property served as many things, including home to the Jamestown Club for Men. The property is currently being used as an office, but it could be converted back into a home, or a high-end bed and breakfast. The property features stunning architecture that is a rare find, along with some of the original ornate woodwork, stained glass windows, and fireplaces. There is a mixture of gorgeous hardwood floors, high end carpet, and even some marble tile throughout the building. The main staircase sits as a centerpiece providing access to the second and third floor, but there are private stair cases as well. With a dream and a solid plan, this could be a rather spacious home, again! Entering through the double doors off the grand hall to the formal living room. What is now the conference room would make a gorgeous formal dining room. Imagine putting in a gourmet kitchen on the first floor, and the kitchenette could be a walk-in pantry or even a laundry room. This is a magnificent, must-see property, words and photos don’t do it justice!","facts":[["Total rooms","20"],["Full baths","0"],["Half baths","3"],["Style","Victorian"],["Stories","3"],["Building area (sq ft)","9,097"],["Heating","Gas, Forced Air"],["Cooling","Central Air"],["Basement","Full, Partia